[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087171886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109875#issuecomment-4087171886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109875","id":4087171886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7znUsu","user":{"login":"Mervius","id":11022926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDIyOTI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11022926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius","html_url":"https://github.com/Mervius","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T02:26:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T03:29:09Z","body":"So, what is the intended method to choose where the window appears? Wayland isn't exactly super great for window positioning.\r\n\r\nYou can technically move the window position after it's open, but that's janky.\r\n\r\nI suppose you could also maybe use a fullscreen window with passthrough then position within that window with a passthrough rect.\r\n\r\nMaybe I'm just missing how the anchors for the layer are set, though...\r\n\r\nI also can't figure out how to move the root window at runtime or before it appears... only subwindows...\r\nThis would probably be essential for a proper application launcher or other overlay tool that is started via a keybind since that root window will always exist afaik without more modifications to godot's source ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087171886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087546024","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109875#issuecomment-4087546024","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109875","id":4087546024,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zowCo","user":{"login":"MoutonDemocrate","id":85873312,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODczMzEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85873312?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate","html_url":"https://github.com/MoutonDemocrate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MoutonDemocrate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T03:36:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T03:36:09Z","body":"> So, what is the intended method to choose where the window appears? Wayland isn't exactly super great for window positioning.\n> \n> You can technically move the window position after it's open, but that's janky.\n> \n> I suppose you could also maybe use a fullscreen window with passthrough then position within that window with a passthrough rect.\n> \n> Maybe I'm just missing how the anchors for the layer are set, though...\n> \n> I also can't figure out how to move the root window at runtime or before it appears... only subwindows...\n> This would probably be essential for a proper application launcher or other overlay tool that is started via a keybind since that root window will always exist afaik without more modifications to godot's source \n\nHey! First, thanks for reminding me I need to work on my half-assed PR. I genuinely forgot it existed.\n\nCurrently, since Wayland uses an anchor+offsets method to position windows, I think I'm just translating window cartesian coordinates to anchor-offset. It's worked quite well to move windows, but also I don't think I actually have tried to move the main window.\n\nI'll add that to my list of things to test and make better. I'm sure my addiction to Pacific Drive is temporary and will eventually subside, after which I'll work on this implementation again.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087546024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087649437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109875#issuecomment-4087649437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109875","id":4087649437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zpJSd","user":{"login":"Mervius","id":11022926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDIyOTI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11022926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius","html_url":"https://github.com/Mervius","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mervius/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T03:57:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T04:04:13Z","body":"Yeah, when I try to move the root window when its set to anything but \"normal\", it doesn't visibly move, but nodes like buttons do seem to think they're in the new position with where they respond to mouse locations...\r\n\r\nIt also seems impossible to focus a window that is anything but \"normal\", meaning keyboard shortcuts couldn't work either., though maybe that's not really an issue and I'm missing the \"proper\" way to do that.\r\n\r\nEDIT: nvm, keyboard focus is supposed to be a thing with `zwlr_layer_surface_v1::keyboard_interactivity`","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087649437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5412454345","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109875#issuecomment-5412454345","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109875","id":5412454345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQpt_yQ","user":{"login":"debugging-in-prod","id":31667253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjY3MjUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31667253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/debugging-in-prod","html_